1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:03,180
They don’t wear uniforms,

2
00:00:04,520 --> 00:00:05,700
they don’t wave flags,

3
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:07,981
but they decide

4
00:00:11,521 --> 00:00:12,621
where the storm begins

5
00:00:14,641 --> 00:00:16,141
and where the world exhales.

6
00:00:21,741 --> 00:00:23,882
They live in shadows under polished logos,

7
00:00:23,942 --> 00:00:26,802
Think tanks whisper - RAND, CSIS, cold and focused.

8
00:00:27,142 --> 00:00:29,222
No armor on, just suits in muted grey,

9
00:00:29,262 --> 00:00:31,842
Counting wars like margins at the end of the day.

10
00:00:32,422 --> 00:00:34,402
No gunfire - just a quiet “Send”,

11
00:00:34,782 --> 00:00:36,982
And somewhere far away the fire starts again.

12
00:00:37,803 --> 00:00:39,783
One signs papers in a glass-lit room,

13
00:00:39,843 --> 00:00:42,523
Another loses home before the afternoon.

14
00:00:43,063 --> 00:00:45,363
They draft scenarios on boring white slides,

15
00:00:45,403 --> 00:00:47,903
Maps where a thin red line decides who survives.

16
00:00:48,403 --> 00:00:50,523
Down here we fight for something called truth,

17
00:00:51,083 --> 00:00:53,064
Up there they price it - by the unit, per use.

18
00:00:53,204 --> 00:00:56,784
The architects build without faces,

19
00:00:58,544 --> 00:01:03,904
They don’t need flags - they believe in numbers.

20
00:01:03,944 --> 00:01:08,125
They whisper to fate like programmers of sleep:

21
00:01:08,145 --> 00:01:21,825
“Load the chaos… let the country run.”

22
00:01:22,286 --> 00:01:25,606
Ooh… let it run

23
00:01:26,346 --> 00:01:30,746
Ah… let it hum

24
00:01:30,766 --> 00:01:38,587
Since two-thousand-eight they’ve been wiring fear,

25
00:01:39,047 --> 00:01:41,227
Crisis as pattern, panic as gear.

26
00:01:41,287 --> 00:01:43,967
Pandemics, wars, currencies, oil,

27
00:01:44,027 --> 00:01:46,567
Every line obeyed, no human recoil.

28
00:01:46,687 --> 00:01:49,307
When the system cracks, no noise, no sound,

29
00:01:49,327 --> 00:01:51,948
They hit “Rebuild” and spin it back around.

30
00:01:52,228 --> 00:01:54,528
Faces may change, but the code stays tight,

31
00:01:54,588 --> 00:01:57,248
No revolution edits that script overnight.

32
00:01:57,568 --> 00:01:59,888
Deep state murmurs, lobbyist hands,

33
00:02:00,268 --> 00:02:02,688
Geopolitics - a garage-band plan.

34
00:02:02,728 --> 00:02:05,248
They don’t need thrones, they don’t need crowns,

35
00:02:05,288 --> 00:02:07,869
Just keys to the rooms where the future’s drawn.

36
00:02:07,909 --> 00:02:11,509
The architects build without faces,

37
00:02:13,229 --> 00:02:18,589
They don’t need flags - they believe in numbers.

38
00:02:18,609 --> 00:02:22,810
They whisper to fate like programmers of sleep:

39
00:02:22,830 --> 00:02:34,910
“Load the chaos… let the country run.”

40
00:02:35,950 --> 00:02:40,351
Ooh… let it run

41
00:02:41,011 --> 00:02:49,211
Ah… but we remain

42
00:02:50,451 --> 00:02:53,012
I see the pattern - not paranoia,

43
00:02:53,112 --> 00:02:55,952
A graph of layers, not noise on noise.

44
00:02:55,972 --> 00:02:57,252
Two-thousand-eight: launch.

45
00:02:57,272 --> 00:02:58,892
Two-thousand-fourteen: shock.

46
00:02:58,912 --> 00:02:59,912
Twenty-twenty: virus.

47
00:02:59,932 --> 00:03:01,732
Twenty-twenty-two: the lock.

48
00:03:01,772 --> 00:03:03,772
They don’t hide - they’re just unseen,

49
00:03:03,792 --> 00:03:06,713
Their truths live quietly in spreadsheets clean.

50
00:03:06,873 --> 00:03:09,273
I don’t run, I don’t freeze,

51
00:03:09,593 --> 00:03:12,193
Reading the system, I become the ease.

52
00:03:12,213 --> 00:03:14,773
I don’t fight - I decode,

53
00:03:15,033 --> 00:03:16,993
Where there’s chaos, I find a road.

54
00:03:17,093 --> 00:03:19,713
If they build fear from days and nights,

55
00:03:19,813 --> 00:03:22,374
I build meaning from people and light.

56
00:03:22,394 --> 00:03:25,174
They sketch reality in pencil lines,

57
00:03:25,194 --> 00:03:27,854
Then erase borrowed dreams with a sharper design.

58
00:03:27,874 --> 00:03:30,534
But I hold the pen - this page is mine,

59
00:03:30,554 --> 00:03:31,954
Where a human’s not an object,

60
00:03:31,974 --> 00:03:33,694
But the context of time.

61
00:03:36,074 --> 00:03:39,515
The architects build without faces,

62
00:03:41,395 --> 00:03:45,015
But hearts don’t run on numbers.

63
00:03:46,555 --> 00:03:51,576
They whisper to fate - we answer in song:

64
00:03:51,596 --> 00:03:56,816
“We are still here… and we carry on.”

65
00:03:56,876 --> 00:03:58,076
Na-na… ooh…

66
00:04:07,217 --> 00:04:07,717
Carry on…

67
00:04:09,457 --> 00:04:13,177
Architects, I read your code.

68
00:04:13,197 --> 00:04:16,677
It works - but still, I stand and breathe.

69
00:04:19,417 --> 00:04:20,957
You manufacture fear,

70
00:04:22,438 --> 00:04:23,458
I choose to love.

71
00:04:24,478 --> 00:04:25,698
And even in the storm,

72
00:04:27,338 --> 00:04:30,918
I stay human.

